<% content_for :title, "Privacy Policy — Spens" %>
<% content_for :description, "What data Spens collects, why, where it is kept and how to have it deleted." %>

<main class="landing-sect legal">
  <div class="landing-container landing-container--narrow">
    <p class="legal__back"><%= link_to "← Spens", landing_path %></p>

    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="legal__updated">Last updated: November 24, 2026</p>

    <p>
      Spens is a personal pocket ledger: you record your transactions, budgets, savings goals, debts
      and accounts in it. This data is sensitive by nature, and this policy explains in plain terms
      what we collect, why, and what we never do with it.
    </p>

    <h2>1. Who is responsible for your data</h2>
    <p>
      Spens is published by David Dossou, acting as an individual. For any question about your data
      or to exercise your rights, write to
      <a href="mailto:djidenou@hey.com">djidenou@hey.com</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>2. What we collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Account data</strong> — your email address and first name (and, if you provide them, your last name and phone number), used to create your account and sign you in. Sign-in uses a one-time code sent by email: we store no passwords.</li>
      <li><strong>Financial data you enter</strong> — transactions (amounts, categories, descriptions, dates), budgets, goals, debts and accounts. This data exists only because you type it in; Spens does not connect to your banks.</li>
      <li><strong>Quick add</strong> — when you describe a transaction in one sentence, it is first analyzed by our own rules, on our servers. When those rules are not enough, <strong>the sentence alone</strong> is sent to Anthropic's Claude AI model to extract the amount, type and category. Your name, email and accounts are never sent to it. Anthropic does not use this data to train its models.</li>
      <li><strong>Voice dictation</strong> — the microphone button uses your phone's own speech recognition (Google on Android, Apple on iOS), only when you tap it. Only the transcribed text reaches us: we never receive or keep any audio recording.</li>
      <li><strong>Reminders and emails</strong> — if you turn them on, reminders are sent to you as notifications (through your browser's or phone's notification service) and/or by email. We also send a few onboarding emails (welcome, tips), which you can unsubscribe from at any time from any of them.</li>
      <li><strong>Usage measurement</strong> — we measure how Spens is used (pages viewed, actions in the app) with PostHog, linked to your account, to understand what works and improve the service. <strong>Your amounts and transactions are not included.</strong></li>
      <li><strong>Technical data</strong> — what is needed to run the service: a session cookie, your device's time zone, and server logs.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      <strong>Advertising cookies.</strong> If you accept them through the cookie banner, we use the
      Meta Pixel and Meta's Conversions API to measure how our campaigns perform (for example, knowing
      that a sign-up came from a Facebook ad). Your email is sent in encrypted (hashed) form. Without
      your consent, nothing is sent to Meta. You can change your mind at any time. In any case,
      <strong>your financial data is never shared with advertising networks</strong>.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Why we process it (legal bases)</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Performance of the service</strong> (GDPR art. 6.1.b) — storing and displaying your financial data, signing you in, running quick add, reminders and shared spaces.</li>
      <li><strong>Legitimate interest</strong> (GDPR art. 6.1.f) — service security, abuse prevention, technical logs, usage measurement to improve Spens, onboarding emails.</li>
      <li><strong>Consent</strong> (GDPR art. 6.1.a) — for voice dictation (the microphone is only ever used on your explicit action), notifications and advertising cookies.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Your data is never sold or rented, and your financial data is never used for advertising.</p>

    <h2>4. Shared spaces</h2>
    <p>
      If you join a shared space (for example with your family), the transactions and budgets of that
      space are visible to its members. You choose what you record in a shared space; your personal
      spaces remain private.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Where your data lives and who helps us</h2>
    <p>
      Your data is hosted on Hetzner servers located in the <strong>United States</strong>. To run
      Spens, we rely on a few providers, each limited to what it needs:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Hetzner</strong> (Germany, servers located in the United States) — server and database hosting.</li>
      <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> (United States) — domain name, protection and routing of traffic to our servers.</li>
      <li><strong>Brevo</strong> (France) — sending emails (sign-in codes, invitations, reminders, onboarding emails).</li>
      <li><strong>Anthropic</strong> (United States) — analyzing quick-add sentences when our rules are not enough.</li>
      <li><strong>PostHog</strong> (United States) — usage measurement.</li>
      <li><strong>Meta</strong> (United States) — measuring advertising campaigns, only with your consent.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Your data is therefore stored and processed outside the European Union, mainly in the United
      States. These transfers are covered by the safeguards provided for by the GDPR (the European Commission's
      standard contractual clauses or the EU–US Data Privacy Framework).
    </p>

    <h2>6. How long we keep it</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Your data is kept for as long as your account is active.</li>
      <li>If you <strong>delete your account</strong>, all of your data is permanently erased. Backup copies are purged within 30 days at most.</li>
      <li>Technical logs are kept for a limited time for security purposes, then deleted.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>7. Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Under the GDPR and applicable data protection laws (including, for users in Côte d'Ivoire, law
      no. 2013-450 on the protection of personal data), you have the rights of access, rectification,
      erasure, portability, restriction and objection over your data.
    </p>
    <p>
      To exercise them, write to <a href="mailto:djidenou@hey.com">djidenou@hey.com</a>. You can also
      delete your account yourself from your profile, which erases all your data. You also have the
      right to lodge a complaint with your supervisory authority (the CNIL in France, the ARTCI in
      Côte d'Ivoire).
    </p>

    <h2>8. Security</h2>
    <p>
      Connections are encrypted (HTTPS), sign-in is passwordless with one-time codes, and server
      access is restricted. No system is infallible, so if an incident ever affects your data we will
      notify you without delay, as required by law.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      This policy may evolve, in particular when new features launch. If a
      significant change is made, you will be informed in the app or by email.
    </p>
  </div>
</main>
